  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Harnessing Community Engagement for Accountable Humanitarian Efforts in the DRC</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to improve the responsiveness, accountability, and impact of humanitarian actions in North and South Kivu by building upon existing feedback mechanisms and expanding their purposes to assure community engagement in each part of the response. This UNICEF project will make the U-Report platform, which facilitates online engagement, and U-Report Communities, which offers face-to-face engagement, available to the AAP Working Group for the humanitarian response. This project also aims to improve the use of U-Report as a feedback tool and platform for internally displaced persons and host communities in the two provinces. The project provides humanitarian assistance to almost 548,000 people, including over 136,600 women and over 312,000 children.</narrative>
  </description>
